 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nmodifying the retirement program for Triborough bridge and tunnel members",
    "basePrintNo": "S6976",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6976-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §604-c, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6976\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nmodifying the retirement program for Triborough bridge and tunnel\nmembers\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo eliminate the requirement to reach 50 years of age in the NYCERS\n20/50 plans for Triborough Bridge and Tunnel Authority employees.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill amends section 604-c of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to eliminate the age 50 qualifier in the 20 Year/Age\n50 Retirement Plan for tier 4 and tier 6 members of the Triborough\nBridge and Tunnel Authority.\n\nSection two set the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would remove the requirement that a Tier 4 or Tier 6 employee\nof the Triborough Bridge and Tunnel Authority (TBTA), or MTA Bridges and\nTunnels, enrolled in NYCERS 20/50 plan reach 50 years of age before\nbecoming eligible to receive a full service retirement.  This bill if\nenacted would allow any Tier 4 or Tier 6 member to receive a full\npension after 20 years of service, regardless of age.  Tier 4 members\nwith at least five years of service, currently able to receive a\nreduced, vested benefit on the date they would have attained 20/50, will\nbe eligible for the vested benefit on the date they would have attained\n20 years of service regardless of age. Tier 6 members with at least ten\nyears of service, currently able to receive a reduced, vested benefit at\nage 63, would continue to be eligible for the vested benefit at age 63.\n\nThis bill will allow younger TBTA employees, who may reach their 20th\nyear of service well before their 50th birthday, to retire at an earlier\nage and will thus lower the payroll obligations for the MTA.  Addi-\ntionally, allowing employees to retire upon their 20th year of service,\nby which point Tier 4 members are no longer contributing anything to\ntheir pensions out of gross wages, also has the potential for long-term\ncost savings for the NYC Employees' Retirement System. These employees\ngenerally retire at lower salaries and thus receive smaller pension\nbenefits than if they had remained employed until reaching age 50.\n\n \nPRIOR_LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
